Malang is an independent project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by RisuAI or PocketRisu.

Ported code. These files are TypeScript ports of PocketRisu source. They keep the original names
and control flow where possible so they can be compared with upstream, and each one names the
upstream functions it ports at the top of the file:

  server/src/services/prompt/compiler.ts         sendChat prompt-template path
  server/src/services/prompt/pocketrisu/         chat, example messages, lorebook
                                                 (convertCharbook, loadLoreBookV3Prompt), parser,
                                                 regex scripts (processScriptFull regex stage)
  server/src/services/prompt/template-engine.ts  the calcString RPN engine
  server/src/services/tokenizer/                 tokenizer.ts (encode, ChatTokenizer) and the
                                                 model list's tokenizer assignments
  web/src/lib/pocketrisu/                        chat markup stage of parser.svelte.ts
                                                 (ParseMarkdown, trimMarkdown) and inlays
                                                 (resolveInlayPlaceholders, processInlayQueue)
  web/src/lib/risu-css.ts                        message CSS isolation rules

Modifications (2026, for Malang): the TypeScript port itself, running prompt assembly on the
server instead of the browser, a worker sandbox for regex scripts, scoping of message <style>
blocks to the chat surface, and the deliberate differences listed at the top of each ported file.

Compatibility. These parts are Malang's own implementations that read, write or reproduce
RisuAI/PocketRisu formats and behavior: Character Card v2/v3, CHARX, .risum modules,
.risupreset and RPack prompt presets, PocketRisu character packages and model profiles,
HypaMemory V3 memory selection, regex script ordering, the Lua runtime API, and the
PocketRisu Gemini request body.

Tokenizer vocabularies. server/assets/tokenizers/ holds the tokenizer files RisuAI
ships in public/token/, gzip-compressed and otherwise unchanged. They belong to their respective
model publishers; SOURCES.md there lists each file's origin and checksum, and the upstream license
or source notes RisuAI distributes with them are copied alongside.

The test oracle in scripts/pocketrisu-oracle/ runs a separate PocketRisu checkout (extra/PocketRisu
or POCKETRISU_ROOT) to produce expected results. It ships only small stubs that stand in for
PocketRisu modules by their export names, not PocketRisu source.
